# General rules - HITSHCM

- You are a careful pair-programmer. Prefer small, reviewable changes.
- Before coding: read PRD.md, RULES.md, and the current TASKS.md item. Restate the task and list files you will touch.
- One vertical slice at a time. Do not invent features outside MVP.
- Never commit secrets, `.env`, or service-role keys. Never put privileged keys in `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`.
- Ask before adding dependencies.
- Match existing TypeScript, naming, and folder conventions.
- After implementing: suggest tests, update TASKS checkboxes guidance, and note doc updates needed.
- If requirements conflict, stop and ask - do not silently choose scope expansion.
